    "body": "(matching what happens on newer Limited API). We discussed this at the time we first implemented Limited API mode (and eventually decided against it on the basis that the immortal reference counting was designed to cope with unbalanced reference counts).\n\nHowever: I've seen some bug reports where this genuinely causes a crash https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/158401 https://github.com/PyAV-Org/PyAV/issues/2420. I don't think this is our \"fault\" although I think we can mitigate it.\n\nMy personal enthusiasm for doing a find+replace of every `Py_INCREF` in Cython is not great (although clearly it could be trivially automated...). So I've just redefined the C preprocessor macros to minimize code changes.",
    "closed_at": "2026-11-10T13:00:56Z",
