                },
                "message": "Use IncRef/DecRef functions on old Limited API\n\n(matching what happens on newer Limited API). We discussed this\nat the time we first implemented Limited API mode (and eventually\ndecided against it on the basis that the immortal reference\ncounting was designed to cope with unbalanced reference counts).\n\nHowever: I've seen some bug reports where this genuinely\ncauses a crash https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/158401\nhttps://github.com/PyAV-Org/PyAV/issues/2420. I don't think this\nis our \"fault\" although I think we can mitigate it.\n\nMy personal enthusiasm for doing a find+replace of every\n`Py_INCREF` in Cython is not great (although clearly it could be\ntrivially automated...). So I've just redefined the C preprocessor\nmacros to minimize code changes.",
